                        "sense_id": "89b50e53-37d4-3fb5-9b97-eab7fddc096f",
                        "entry_id": "558fa7b5-1e71-3b82-92d6-c54c2240a9ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Blurred, hazy, indistinct, unfocussed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Northern-England",
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4238c2db-694c-4d43-8481-b9d2d29bd43e",
                                "sense_id": "89b50e53-37d4-3fb5-9b97-eab7fddc096f",
                                "text": "The Handel excerpts are afflicted with a combination of high surface noise from the source material as well as variably muzzy sound."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d8f1b40b-0f1a-3f1e-a559-fd301492de5c",
                        "entry_id": "558fa7b5-1e71-3b82-92d6-c54c2240a9ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bewildered; dazed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9204663f-aaa6-3ea4-a76e-77b3a6840a77",
                        "entry_id": "558fa7b5-1e71-3b82-92d6-c54c2240a9ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tipsy; drunk; involving drunkenness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53591d39-5ca1-4191-94b9-a3409852707b",
                                "sense_id": "9204663f-aaa6-3ea4-a76e-77b3a6840a77",
                                "text": "Why laſt night, as Colonel Kill'em, Sir William Weezy, Lord Frederick Foretop, and I were careleſsly ſliding the Ranelagh round, picking our teeth, after a damn'd muzzy dinner at Boodle's, who ſhould trip by but an abbeſs, well known about town, with a ſmart little nun in her ſuite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ed8f838-a343-449b-861b-e0c5b3cab814",
                                "sense_id": "9204663f-aaa6-3ea4-a76e-77b3a6840a77",
                                "text": "To the muzzy drumming of beer in his veins he gazed long and owlishly at the sombre cottage[.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8293f49-c9c3-49e2-9d32-ed5e8d19ac37",
                                "sense_id": "9204663f-aaa6-3ea4-a76e-77b3a6840a77",
                                "text": "The front bar was plying trade too, by customers that kept oozing in through the back door. The fat publican served whoever came, muzzy with the succession of pots that stodged away his day."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
